WEBVTT

00:02.498 --> 00:05.865
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.968 --> 00:09.200
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.306 --> 00:12.867
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.976 --> 00:15.946
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:16.047 --> 00:19.210
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.317 --> 00:22.582
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.687 --> 00:24.121
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.222 --> 00:25.849
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.991 --> 00:30.758
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.468 --> 00:37.868
<i>We now return
to How I Met Your Father.</i>

00:37.971 --> 00:40.998
<i>Oh, Barney, I'm never going to
meet the right girl and get married.</i>

00:41.108 --> 00:43.076
<i>You know, Ted,
don't you think it's kind of strange</i>

00:43.177 --> 00:44.940
<i>for a guy in his 20s to always be talking</i>

00:45.045 --> 00:48.014
<i>about getting married,
rather than getting laid?</i>

00:48.115 --> 00:52.485
<i>- Barney, I'm in love with you.
- Suit up!</i>

00:55.123 --> 00:58.389
All right, come on, everyone.
Go get dressed. It's ballet night.

01:00.196 --> 01:02.460
Lois, don't freaking put me
through this again.

01:02.565 --> 01:05.033
Peter, a little culture is
good for this family.

01:05.134 --> 01:07.262
<i>Besides, you liked The Nutcracker,
didn't you?</i>

01:07.371 --> 01:11.467
<i>No, Lois, I did not.
The Nutcracker had zero physical comedy.</i>

01:11.575 --> 01:13.133
<i>And with a name like The Nutcracker,</i>

01:13.276 --> 01:15.108
I thought,
"Oh, this'll be worth a few yucks. "

01:15.213 --> 01:17.408
But, no, Lois, that title wrote a check

01:17.515 --> 01:19.847
that those queers on stage
refused to cash.

01:19.951 --> 01:21.179
Peter, we're going.

01:21.319 --> 01:24.414
Well, we're not the first people
to be dragged off against our will.

01:24.723 --> 01:26.054
- Are we there yet?
- No!

01:26.191 --> 01:27.522
- Are we there yet?
- No!

01:27.626 --> 01:29.560
- Are we there yet?
- Damn it, I swear to God,

01:29.661 --> 01:31.823
I will turn this ship around!

01:31.998 --> 01:32.987
- That works.
- Okay.

01:33.099 --> 01:34.964
- Lf you want to teach us a lesson...
- Yeah, that's even better.

01:35.068 --> 01:37.229
All right, if that's what you...
Wait a minute!

01:42.576 --> 01:48.208
You know, Meg, female ballet dancers
are famous for anorexia and bulimia and...

01:48.316 --> 01:50.216
It seems to work out for them.

01:50.318 --> 01:53.446
So... Hintedy-hint-hint.

01:53.588 --> 01:55.283
Boy, this is gonna be long.

01:55.390 --> 01:58.485
So, you kids develop
any good pot connections

01:58.594 --> 01:59.754
- at your school yet?
- What?

01:59.862 --> 02:02.092
- Yeah.
- Lois, we'll be right back.

02:02.198 --> 02:04.723
Meg's gonna take me outside to poop.

02:21.670 --> 02:23.229
<i>Hello?
- Hey, Quagmire.</i>

02:23.340 --> 02:26.309
<i>- Hey, Peter, what's up?
- I'm stuck at the stupid ballet.</i>

02:26.410 --> 02:27.900
<i>- Get out of here. You serious?
- Yeah.</i>

02:28.011 --> 02:29.205
<i>- So am I!
- What?</i>

02:29.312 --> 02:30.370
<i>Yeah, I got dragged here
by this broad I'm trying to screw.</i>

02:30.480 --> 02:31.470
Where you sitting?

02:31.582 --> 02:32.549
<i>Look across
at the other balcony,</i>

02:32.650 --> 02:33.639
<i>I can see you.</i>

02:36.851 --> 02:38.045
Oh, my God! What do we do?
What do we do?

02:38.152 --> 02:39.120
What do we do? We're both here.

02:39.254 --> 02:41.779
Oh, my God, we should text each other.
Hang up! Hang up!

03:00.953 --> 03:04.252
Chris, how many times have I told you,
no reading during meals.

03:04.357 --> 03:05.984
I have a history test today, Mom,

03:06.092 --> 03:10.290
and I couldn't study last night
because you made us go to the ballet.

03:14.101 --> 03:15.693
Yeah, right in her ass.

03:19.206 --> 03:21.402
Well, Chris, you're not gonna learn
any history from this.

03:21.510 --> 03:24.479
- This textbook is from 1896.
- What?

03:24.579 --> 03:28.811
- "Chapter Three. Here Comes Utah. "
- Let me see that.

03:29.251 --> 03:33.188
"Negroes, America's Dancingest
Rapefolk. " That's awful!

03:33.289 --> 03:34.313
We don't use the word "negro" anymore.

03:36.279 --> 03:37.439
What the hell?
Are these schools so underfunded

03:37.547 --> 03:39.709
that they can't afford textbooks
from this century?

03:39.817 --> 03:43.014
Well, I am gonna raise hell about this
at the next PTA meeting.

03:43.120 --> 03:45.816
Well, let me know if you need help.
I can be very persuasive.

03:45.923 --> 03:48.688
<i>I gave the next speech
after the Braveheart guy.</i>

03:48.794 --> 03:54.289
They can take our lives,
but they can never take our freedom!

03:55.668 --> 03:59.729
And, and, let's not forget the tax
they levied on properties

03:59.839 --> 04:04.436
that are in abutment of church lands.
So, yeah! Let's do it!

04:10.784 --> 04:12.685
All right, let's get this meeting underway.

04:12.787 --> 04:15.722
For our first order of business,
we'll go to Bruce.

04:15.824 --> 04:18.452
Oh, hey, y'all said my name!

04:18.560 --> 04:20.859
Welcome to our meeting
here at the school.

04:20.963 --> 04:23.625
We've got lots
of exciting topics here tonight.

04:23.732 --> 04:26.792
We gonna have a puppet show,
we gonna have some jazz.

04:26.902 --> 04:28.199
No, I'm just kidding.

04:28.304 --> 04:30.773
We have some business
to take care of, though.

04:30.874 --> 04:32.865
I'm sorry I pulled y'alls legs.

04:32.976 --> 04:36.673
I'm just a little excited
'cause I met somebody today.

04:36.780 --> 04:38.749
Someone in the bookstore.

04:38.850 --> 04:42.081
Someone who likes
the same kind of literature as I do.

04:42.186 --> 04:44.620
Oh, and the adventure begins again.

04:44.722 --> 04:47.920
Excuse me, Principal Shepherd,
there's something I'd like to discuss.

04:48.026 --> 04:50.620
The school has gone too far
with these budget cuts.

04:50.729 --> 04:53.527
I'm sorry, Mrs. Griffin,
but the "No Child Left Behind" law

04:53.632 --> 04:55.123
cost us our federal funding

04:55.268 --> 04:57.361
because our students' test scores
were too low.

04:57.470 --> 05:00.735
They cut a school's funding
if it's got low test scores?

05:00.840 --> 05:03.537
This is not what the founding fathers
had in mind.

05:03.777 --> 05:07.213
Okay, we're here to sign this declaration
of our independence.

05:07.314 --> 05:08.747
Let's take roll call first.

05:08.849 --> 05:10.282
- Thomas Jefferson?
Here.

05:10.384 --> 05:11.943
- Benjamin Franklin?
Here.

05:12.053 --> 05:14.453
- John Footpenis?
It's Hancock now.

05:14.556 --> 05:15.523
Why?

05:15.624 --> 05:16.613
Mind your business,
that's why.

05:16.925 --> 05:20.487
Well, somehow this school needs
to raise its test scores right away!

05:20.596 --> 05:24.362
I suppose there is one thing I can do
to raise the school's test average.

05:24.467 --> 05:25.491
Then do it!

05:25.601 --> 05:28.594
All right.
We'll drop the dumbest student we have.

05:28.705 --> 05:31.435
Chris Griffin is hereby expelled.

05:31.541 --> 05:35.272
But if I leave now, I won't hear
who's the dumbest kid in the school.

05:40.919 --> 05:45.550
Cool, I don't have to go to school.
I can just pee in my bed all day.

05:45.691 --> 05:48.023
Chris, being expelled is a serious thing.

05:48.127 --> 05:50.254
Peter, we've got to find another school
for him.

05:50.362 --> 05:51.829
I say, I could home-school him.

05:51.931 --> 05:54.332
After all, I taught Cleveland
how to make Jiffy Pop.

05:55.669 --> 05:56.636
Oh!

06:04.378 --> 06:06.642
So, do you think
your school would be right for Chris?

06:06.747 --> 06:08.112
Oh, absolutely.

06:08.215 --> 06:10.582
Quahog School for the Deaf
has great programs,

06:10.686 --> 06:12.244
both academic and athletic.

06:12.354 --> 06:15.482
In fact, you're just in time
for our homecoming pep rally.

06:15.590 --> 06:18.992
- What are we gonna do to Lincoln?
Kill them!

06:19.095 --> 06:22.155
- I can't hear you!
Kill them!

06:22.265 --> 06:25.632
- I can't hear you!
Kill them!

06:25.735 --> 06:28.967
- I can't hear you!
Kill them!

06:29.073 --> 06:32.406
- I can't hear you!
Kill them!

06:32.509 --> 06:33.476
Let's just go.

06:36.815 --> 06:39.249
Welcome to
the Quahog Maritime School, Chris.

06:39.351 --> 06:43.583
Our curriculum consists of being on boats
for long periods of time with men.

06:43.722 --> 06:46.021
Just men. For many days at a time.

06:46.125 --> 06:50.118
Up on the deck with lots of men,
or down in the galley with lots of men.

06:50.229 --> 06:52.129
Is this some kind of pirate school?

06:52.231 --> 06:55.759
Well, a certain kind of pirate.
Yes, we've been called that.

06:55.869 --> 06:59.236
- I don't know.
- Is there some kind of pre-school program?

07:02.143 --> 07:03.201
You know, I have to admit,

07:03.311 --> 07:05.142
I've always been a little worried
about Chris,

07:05.246 --> 07:08.909
but I guess I just convinced myself
things would work out for him.

07:09.017 --> 07:12.181
But with no education,
what kind of future can he possibly have?

07:12.287 --> 07:13.584
Well, what are we supposed to do, Lois?

07:13.689 --> 07:15.714
I mean, it's not like the high school
will take him back.

07:15.824 --> 07:19.727
And every other school we've tried
just doesn't... Oh, crap!

09:15.958 --> 09:17.358
My son got into DeVry.

09:17.461 --> 09:21.022
Oh, good, what'd he have to do,
open the door?

09:21.131 --> 09:23.429
Can't you let me have anything?

10:13.590 --> 10:18.324
Wait, wait, wait. Hang on, hang on.
What are we fighting about?

10:18.429 --> 10:20.761
- You know, I have completely forgotten.
- Me, too.

10:20.864 --> 10:22.525
Something about a coupon?

10:22.633 --> 10:25.899
- I cannot for the life of me remember.
- Oh, my God, that's ridiculous.

10:26.004 --> 10:28.063
You know what,
I just... I hope I didn't hurt you

10:28.173 --> 10:30.801
- because I'd feel terrible about that.
- No, no, no. I'm all right.

10:30.909 --> 10:32.571
But, listen, you know what,
let me make it up to you.

10:32.712 --> 10:34.043
Why don't you let my wife and I
take you out to dinner.

10:34.146 --> 10:35.135
Well, that sounds lovely.

10:39.619 --> 10:40.813
That was delicious.

10:40.920 --> 10:42.650
You know, I drive by this place all the time

10:42.756 --> 10:44.724
and I've never been inside,
isn't that funny?

10:44.825 --> 10:47.555
Yeah, you know,
Nicole and I came here by accident.

10:47.661 --> 10:49.857
We had reservations at another place
and they...

10:49.964 --> 10:51.659
- Right, right, honey?
- Yeah. They couldn't seat us

10:51.766 --> 10:53.393
for, like, an hour,
so we ended up coming here

10:53.501 --> 10:54.661
- and we just loved it.
- Loved it.

10:54.769 --> 10:57.033
I can see why. I mean, that halibut was...

10:57.138 --> 10:59.767
That may have been the best halibut
I've ever had.

10:59.875 --> 11:01.536
Well, I'm glad we talked you out
of the pork chops, huh?

11:01.644 --> 11:04.579
Yes! Thank you!

11:04.680 --> 11:06.546
Oh, oh, let me, let me, let... I'll get that.
I'll get that.

11:06.650 --> 11:09.585
- Oh, no, no, no, no. I got it.
- No, no, no, no, no. I'm taking care of this.

11:09.686 --> 11:11.586
No, no, no, your money's no good here.

11:11.688 --> 11:13.679
No, my food was more expensive.
I feel bad if...

11:13.790 --> 11:15.656
We invited you. I've got this.

11:15.760 --> 11:18.092
- Look, just let go of the check.
- You let go of the check.

11:18.195 --> 11:21.494
- I'm not taking my hand off this thing.
- Well, neither am I.

11:21.599 --> 11:23.089
Let go of the check.

11:23.200 --> 11:24.793
- Ernie, if he wants to...
- Stay out of this!

11:24.903 --> 11:26.336
Don't you talk to my wife like that!

11:26.438 --> 11:29.134
Oh, yeah?
What are you gonna do about it?

12:31.244 --> 12:32.575
Sorry.

12:32.679 --> 12:33.907
And every other school we've tried

12:34.013 --> 12:35.878
just doesn't seem to be a good fit
for Chris.

12:35.982 --> 12:38.075
Well, there is one other option.

12:41.355 --> 12:43.983
Daddy, there's something I need you
to do for me.

12:44.091 --> 12:46.184
Chris got expelled
from James Woods High,

12:46.293 --> 12:48.626
and, well, I was wondering
if you could get him

12:48.730 --> 12:50.994
into that fancy boarding school
you went to.

12:51.099 --> 12:53.693
You want me to get Chris
into Morningwood Academy?

12:53.802 --> 12:55.827
It would mean so much to our family.

12:55.937 --> 12:58.600
All right, I'll pull some strings
on one condition.

12:58.708 --> 13:01.472
I want Peter
to do something really humiliating.

13:01.577 --> 13:03.477
Well, what did you have in mind?

13:03.579 --> 13:07.414
<i>He has to shoot and star
in a shot-for-shot remake of Liar Liar</i>

13:07.518 --> 13:08.644
for my amusement.

13:08.986 --> 13:10.112
Do you know why I stopped you?

13:10.220 --> 13:12.381
I didn't fasten my seat belt,
I didn't look in my rear view mirror,

13:12.489 --> 13:13.752
I didn't signal when I pulled away
from the curb,

13:13.858 --> 13:15.689
I almost hit a Chevy,
I changed lanes in the intersection

13:15.794 --> 13:19.389
without signaling, I changed lanes
while running a red light and speeding.

13:28.878 --> 13:32.713
- Well, Chris, here we are.
- Wow, this school is really nice.

13:32.816 --> 13:34.078
Boy, a degree from here would set you up
with any job you wanted.

13:35.352 --> 13:38.446
Yes, I should attend this institution.

13:38.555 --> 13:40.786
Perhaps one day I could be more powerful
than King Friday.

13:41.059 --> 13:43.892
I am the supreme ruler
of the Neighborhood of Make-Believe.

13:43.995 --> 13:46.486
All will kneel before...

13:47.800 --> 13:50.564
What kind of freaking king lives
next to the train tracks?

13:50.670 --> 13:52.137
What is this, Mexico?

13:55.676 --> 13:59.908
- Hi, is this Room 214?
- Oh, you must be our new dorm-mate!

14:00.013 --> 14:03.449
I'm Rogers ChapStick,
heir to the ChapStick fortune.

14:03.550 --> 14:07.214
And this is Virgil MasterCard,
heir to the MasterCard fortune.

14:07.321 --> 14:13.693
Oh, yes, yes,
how do you do, sir?

14:13.962 --> 14:16.362
And this is James Bottomtooth IV.

14:19.234 --> 14:22.898
- I'm Chris.
- Let me get those bags for you. Johann?

14:26.509 --> 14:27.476
Um...

14:27.577 --> 14:31.344
Oh, dear. Johann tells me your luggage
is the luggage of the poor.

14:31.449 --> 14:33.815
Well, I am poor.

14:33.918 --> 14:36.409
Oh. Oh, I see.

14:48.101 --> 14:49.068
What the...

14:49.168 --> 14:50.897
Ow! Ow! Ow!

14:52.405 --> 14:55.068
- This school is not for your kind!
- Why?

14:58.645 --> 15:01.136
I still don't fully understand!

15:10.892 --> 15:13.726
And that was the third time
I slept with Katherine Harris.

15:13.829 --> 15:17.060
Well, I love her politics,
but how is she in bed?

15:17.166 --> 15:20.762
Well, as anyone in Florida will tell you,
she knows how to rig an erection.

15:25.075 --> 15:26.565
One time I picked my nose

15:26.676 --> 15:29.305
and I swear
I could feel the bottom of my eye.

15:29.413 --> 15:32.280
- Shut up, poor kid.
- No, I'm serious, look!

15:38.511 --> 15:42.675
- So, Chris, how's the new school?
- It's awful! I hate it!

15:42.782 --> 15:45.250
Everybody's mean to me
because I'm not rich.

15:45.351 --> 15:48.981
Oh, no, Chris, that's horrible.
All right, look, I'll tell you what.

15:49.089 --> 15:51.683
I'll call Daddy and I'll see
if there's anything he can do.

15:51.792 --> 15:53.726
Good, 'cause I haven't been this miserable

15:53.827 --> 15:57.161
since I had to throw Rocky Balboa
out of the Shamrock Meat Company.

15:57.332 --> 16:01.166
Look, I'm sorry, I can't have you in here
punching the meat.

16:01.269 --> 16:03.966
I mean, there's really not too many things
you can't do in here,

16:04.073 --> 16:05.506
but that is one of them.

16:05.607 --> 16:08.371
What about Paulie?
He's having sex with the meat.

16:08.477 --> 16:10.502
- Hey, Rock, I'm porking it.
- That's a good one.

16:14.916 --> 16:15.883
Phew!

16:16.017 --> 16:17.541
Well, that's enough fun for one day.

16:17.652 --> 16:21.020
I'm sweating more
than a non-legacy applying to Yale.

16:45.484 --> 16:46.815
Where am I?

16:48.153 --> 16:50.348
Grandpa? What are you doing here?

16:50.455 --> 16:53.653
Chris, welcome
to the Skull and Bones Society.

16:53.759 --> 16:57.456
This is where the most powerful men
in the world are groomed for their futures.

16:57.597 --> 17:01.533
Every president, every CEO,
every douche bag named Ryan Seacrest.

17:01.635 --> 17:05.435
The Skull and Bones Society
has been a part of my family for decades,

17:05.539 --> 17:07.336
and we want you to become a member.

17:07.441 --> 17:10.605
- Really? Wow, cool!
- Excellent.

17:10.712 --> 17:14.546
You get your own stock portfolio,
a percentage of the 9/11 Victims Fund,

17:14.649 --> 17:18.643
and the best medical care on the planet.
You'll be kept as healthy as a horse.

17:19.622 --> 17:23.023
- So, how's that leg doing?
- Great! Great! Never better!

17:23.159 --> 17:25.150
Good. Why don't you try
putting some weight on it?

17:25.261 --> 17:27.025
Oh, sure.

17:27.130 --> 17:31.362
Yes! Yes! Oh, that's good!
That feels good! Very strong!

17:31.468 --> 17:34.301
Sorry, Thunder, I got to put you down.

17:35.473 --> 17:38.340
How's your leg? Huh? How's your leg?
You ready to race? Huh?

17:44.149 --> 17:45.207
<i>We now return to</i>

17:45.317 --> 17:48.286
Japanese Girls Think
Small Versions of Things Are Really Cute.

17:48.487 --> 17:49.476
<i>Oh!</i>

17:49.588 --> 17:52.113
<i>Look at my tiny dog!
I'm gonna put it in my tiny purse!</i>

17:53.593 --> 17:55.720
<i>Tiny phone! Tiny everything!</i>

17:58.298 --> 18:00.323
Peter, have you seen this tuition bill?

18:00.433 --> 18:03.460
Morningwood Academy
is charging us $30,000.

18:03.571 --> 18:06.335
Well, looks like we're all gonna have
to take second jobs.

18:06.440 --> 18:10.172
I guess I'll see if I can get my old gig back,
selling buttscratchers at the ballpark.

18:10.412 --> 18:13.643
Buttscratcher! Buttscratcher!
Get your buttscratcher here!

18:13.748 --> 18:15.579
- Buttscratcher!
- Buttscratcher?

18:15.684 --> 18:17.652
- Buttscratcher!
- Buttscratcher.

18:17.753 --> 18:18.720
Buttscratcher.

18:18.821 --> 18:20.755
Buttscratcher!
- Buttscratcher!

18:25.494 --> 18:26.928
Chris, come here, you'll love this.

18:27.030 --> 18:29.965
The first Thursday of every month
we go to a local orphanage,

18:30.100 --> 18:33.228
pick out a kid, fill out all the paperwork,
and then don't take him home.

18:33.337 --> 18:36.034
- It's hilarious.
- That sounds kind of cruel.

18:36.140 --> 18:37.732
No, no, you'll love it. It's great.

18:40.245 --> 18:43.738
Come on! Come on in!
Your family's waiting in here!

18:43.849 --> 18:45.908
There are toys and a puppy!

18:46.018 --> 18:48.612
And food that's not served
from warming trays!

18:52.058 --> 18:54.618
Come on! You got to want it!

18:54.728 --> 18:56.593
Oh, you got to do better than that!

18:56.696 --> 19:00.497
Okay, I guess you don't want a new family,
toys and a puppy.

19:05.306 --> 19:07.365
Hi, everybody, I'm home!

19:07.475 --> 19:08.670
- Hi, Chris.
- Hey, how are you?

19:08.777 --> 19:12.304
Well, tell us everything, sweetie.
How's school going so far?

19:12.414 --> 19:13.472
It's great, Mom!

19:13.582 --> 19:16.483
I got powerful connections now,
thanks to Grandpa.

19:16.585 --> 19:17.553
Chris, I'd give you a hug,

19:17.654 --> 19:20.817
but I'm exhausted from working two jobs
to pay your tuition.

19:20.923 --> 19:22.117
I've been selling buttscratchers.

19:22.225 --> 19:23.852
- Buttscratcher!
- No, Peter.

19:23.960 --> 19:25.724
- Buttscratcher!
- Peter, no!

19:25.829 --> 19:27.490
- Buttscratcher!
- No!

19:27.598 --> 19:30.362
- Buttscratcher.
- Dad, you...

19:30.467 --> 19:33.402
You got an extra job
just to put me through school?

19:33.504 --> 19:36.303
We all did, Chris.
Meg and I have been working nights.

19:38.209 --> 19:39.801
I'll take the one on the right!

19:39.911 --> 19:42.779
Well, once again, Meg,
I'll be back in an hour.

19:42.882 --> 19:45.851
And I got a job
following fat people around with a tuba.

19:49.588 --> 19:53.047
Stop it! Cut it out!

19:53.393 --> 19:55.588
I have a glandular problem!

19:57.297 --> 19:58.559
That'll be $60.

20:07.175 --> 20:11.169
- You wanted to see me, Grandpa?
- Yes, Chris. Your pledge period is over.

20:11.313 --> 20:15.010
The Skull and Bones elders are now
ready to admit you to our ranks.

20:15.117 --> 20:17.279
As is customary
with all our new members,

20:17.387 --> 20:19.514
you now have to spend seven minutes
in the closet

20:19.656 --> 20:21.180
with our most senior member.

20:21.291 --> 20:24.488
We don't start the clock
until the door closes.

20:24.595 --> 20:27.189
You know, Grandpa,
I don't think I wanna go through with it.

20:27.298 --> 20:29.289
We all had to do it, Chris.
Now get in there.

20:29.400 --> 20:32.233
No, I mean,
I think I wanna go back to my old school.

20:32.336 --> 20:36.865
My family's working so hard
to pay my tuition here, and I feel bad.

20:37.008 --> 20:40.171
Is there any way you can get me
back into James Woods High?

20:40.278 --> 20:44.375
Well, I suppose I could pull some strings,
if that's really what you want, Chris.

20:44.484 --> 20:47.009
- It is.
- All right, consider it done.

20:47.120 --> 20:48.678
Thanks, Grandpa.

20:50.023 --> 20:52.150
- Sorry, Master Herbert.
- Sorry?

20:52.259 --> 20:55.353
You better get your ass
in that closet, Pewterschmidt.

20:55.462 --> 20:57.430
Yes, sir.

20:57.531 --> 20:59.295
I am so tired of you.

21:03.538 --> 21:05.335
It's good to have you back, buddy.

21:05.440 --> 21:08.103
Thanks, Dad.
I didn't really fit in there anyway.

21:08.210 --> 21:10.405
The rooms were only 15 by 20.

21:13.983 --> 21:16.817
If I didn't learn to laugh at myself,
I'd be dead right now.

21:16.920 --> 21:19.047
Why don't you take your stuff
up to your room, Chris?

21:19.156 --> 21:20.453
Okay, Mom.

21:23.360 --> 21:27.320
Cut it out! I'm just trying to live my life!

21:27.965 --> 21:30.126
No one taught me about carbs!

21:30.127 --> 22:31.127
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru